              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for an airline, then the Persian for a boarding pass."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: گیت",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "گیت (git) — \"a gate (at an airport)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مسافران جلوی گیت شماره پنج صف کشیدند. Mosâferân jolow-ye git-e shomâre-ye panj saf keshidand. The passengers queued in front of gate number five."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also the security gate you walk through."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "git was borrowed from English and is usually traced to English gate. EtymDB does not list the Persian word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
            }
          ]
        },
