        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: گذرنامه",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "گذرنامه (gozarnâme) — \"a passport (formal word)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مامور فرودگاه گذرنامه من را نگاه کرد. Ma'mur-e forudgâh gozarnâme-ye man râ negâh kard. The airport officer looked at my passport."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The formal word; in speech pâsport is more common. gozar 'passing' + nâme 'letter'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "gozarnâme is a native compound, a letter for passing: gozar is the present stem of gozashtan 'to pass', which EtymDB traces to a Middle Persian verb 'to pass, to cross', and nâme 'letter' is usually traced to Middle Persian nāmag."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
